1.5 Summary of Vulnerabilities in CrushFTP [completed]
CrushFTP has critical vulnerabilities including CVE-2025-54309 (Zero-Day, Exploited in the Wild), CVE-2025-2825 / CVE-2025-31161 (Authentication Bypass, Exploited in the Wild), CVE-2023-43177 (Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution), and CVE-2024-4040 (VFS Sandbox Escape / Server-Side Template Injection, Exploited in the Wild). Recommendations include immediate updates to the latest stable versions, implementing DMZ proxy, monitoring for compromise, and network segmentation.}  
